          "totalPages": 16,
          "rawText": "FILE: Oncology-Principle of cancer.pdf\nFOLDER: Chapter 11 Oncology\nDRIVE_URL: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rzDJyNosIV93Yeh8WFYvlsB-Ic25R770/view\nTOTAL_PAGES: 16\n\n--- [Page 1] ---\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\nPHARMA PLUS INSTITUTE\nPRINCIPLE OF \nCANCER THERAPY\n\n--- [Page 2] ---\nCharacteristic of cancer\n2\n■ Increase proliferation \n– Density-dependent inhibition\n– Anchorage independent growth\n■ Decrease apoptosis\n■ Angiogenesis\n■ Invasion\n■ Metastasis\n\n--- [Page 3] ---\nBenign and malignant\n3\nBenign Malignant\n- Not cancer\n- Encapsulated and Localized \n- Seldom Metastasis\n- Cancer\n- Invade neighboring tissue\n- Metastasis\n1  > 2 > 4 > 8 > 16 > 64 …….. Doubling time\n\n--- [Page 4] ---\nCarcinogenesis\n4\nOncogene: ABL, RASK, HER2\nTumor suppressor gene: p53, BRCA1, BRCA2\n\n--- [Page 5] ---\nCell cycle\n5\nKatzung BG, et al. Basic & clinical pharmacology, 12th  ed. 2012.\n\n--- [Page 6] ---\nLog cell kill model\n6\nKatzung Basic and Clinical Pharmacology\n\n--- [Page 7] ---\nStaging of cancer\n7\n■ Solid tumor  eg. Colon cancer, Lung cancer\n TNM classification\n■ T: Tumor size (T1→T4)\n■ N: Lymph node (N0 → N3)\n■ M: Metastasis (M0 →M1)\n■ Hematological malignancies eg. NHL, CML, CLL\n■ Different staging \n■ Not use TNM\n\n--- [Page 8] ---\nTreatment option\n8\n■ Chemotherapy: Systemic treatment\n▪ Adjuvant \n▪ To eradicate micro -metastases following localized \ntreatment\n▪ Potentially curable disease with no clinical \ndetectable disease following surgery or radiation\n▪ Neoadjuvant\n▪ Used to reduce tumor burden (to reduce mass size)\n▪ Usually administered before surgery or radiation\n\n--- [Page 9] ---\nTreatment option\n9\n■ Surgery: Remove tumor for localized treatment\n■ Radiation therapy: Localized treatment\n■ Chemotherapy\n■ Hormone therapy\n■ Targeted therapy\n\n--- [Page 10] ---\nOutcome of treatment\n10\n■ Complete response (CR)\n■ Partial response (PR) \n■ Stable disease (SD) \n■ Progression disease (PD)\n\n--- [Page 11] ---\nOutcome of treatment\n11\nKorean Journal of Radiology eISSN 2005\n\n--- [Page 12] ---\nPatient evaluation\n12\n■ Performance  status\nEastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG)\nBr. J. Cancer (1993), 67, 773-775\n\n--- [Page 13] ---\nPatient evaluation\n13\n■ Underlying disease \n■ Safety factor \n– WBC > 3,000 cell/mm3\n– ANC (Absolute neutrophil count) > 1,500 cell/mm3\n– Hb (Hemoglobin) > 10 g/dl\n– Hct (Hematocrit) > 30 %\n– Platelet > 100,000 cell/mm3\n\n--- [Page 14] ---\nPatient evaluation\n14\n■ Ideal body weight (IBW)\nIBW male    = 50  + {2.3 x[(Ht-150 cm)/2.54]}\nIBW female = 45.5 + {2.3 x[(Ht-150 cm)/2.54]}\n■ Creatinine clearance (CrCl) [ml/min]\nMale = [(140-age)xIBW(kg)]/ 72x Scr\nFemale = {[(140-age)xIBW(kg)]/ 72x Scr}x 0.85\n■ Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC)\nANC = Total WBC x (% Neutrophil + %band)/100\n\n--- [Page 15] ---\nPatient evaluation\n15\n■ Body Surface Area (BSA)\n\n--- [Page 16] ---\n16"
